## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Cardamom capsule, beta-pinene, black pepper, aldehydic rind | Linalyl/linalool seam and Bontoux lavender body | First dry cedar and coumarin shadows | Cardamom arrives first and organizes citrus |
| 5–45 min | Cold shell narrows | Lavender, dihydrojasmone, Jessemal, clary, Leafovert, and Dynascone expose warm seed | Coumarin/Tonkarome, damascenone, heliotropal, immortelle, and a dry bark micro-seam | Warmth is the interior of the same pod, not a second accord |
| 45 min–3 h | Aromatic seed residue | Violet/root cloth and fatty-floral stitches | Three cedar grains, vetiver, and separated sandalwood planes | Tailoring shapes cardamom without iris or leather takeover |
| 3–8 h+ | Dry aromatic grain | Coumarinic wood and creamy skin | Mineral pressure and long dry contour | Ester, seed, cloth, and wood relations recall cardamom after literal top loss |

All temporal language above is design intent, not observed evolution.

