## Missing-chemical impact gate

| Missing exact | Current approximation | Residual limitation | Impact | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cardamom CO2/absolute | Cardamom EO + Terpinyl Acetate + Jessemal + Immortelle 10% | The warm oily crushed-seed interior is less literal and the EO remains more terpenic | **High** for dual-state cardamom realism | Purchase P1 only after the present topology preserves identity and liking |
| Caraway EO | Clary Sage + Terpinyl Acetate + Immortelle 10% | Historic aromatic seed shadow remains approximate; immortelle can drift curry/maple | **Medium** | Purchase P2 only after the warm-handoff module survives |

The NYSUPPLY Cinnamon Bark EO row has no MW/logP/VP values and no natural-mixture decomposition, so its OAV and time-course contribution are `PHYSICS-DATA HOLD`. That gap does not block formula arithmetic, but it blocks any modeled perceptibility, dominance, or temporal claim for the bark. Missing ideal materials separately block claims of literal two-state realism.

## Controlled blinded topology test — future work

Before the 2x2, run a constant-total bark admission pair: **A = V3 minus 10 uL bark + 10 uL DPG**; **B = full V3 with 10 uL NYSUPPLY Cinnamon Bark EO 10%**. Keep every other row identical. Use blind codes and duplicate independently poured samples. Retain B only if it improves warm-seed plausibility and shell-to-seed continuity without cinnamon candy, pastry, harshness, or loss of cardamom leadership. A null or discordant result is `HOLD / NON-INFORMATIVE`; it does not validate the engine's data-driven zero.

Keep the 5,920 uL protected nucleus constant. Omitted modules are replaced one-for-one with DPG; all arms total 6,000 uL concentrate.

- **SEED-HANDOFF+ (50 uL):** Damascenone 1% 20 + Beta Ionone 1% 20 + Immortelle Absolute 10% 10. Tests dried-fruit/bruise/hayed-herbal continuity. Curry, maple, or pastry drift rejects it.
- **TAILORED-RELIEF+ (30 uL):** Beta-Pinene 1% 10 + Dynascone 10% 10 + Orivone 10% 10. Tests capsule edge, bitter-green tailoring, and root-to-wood relief.

| Arm | Protected core | SEED-HANDOFF+ | TAILORED-RELIEF+ | DPG replacement | Total concentrate |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| A / 00 compressed control | 5920 | 0 | 0 | 80 | 6000 |
| B / 10 | 5920 | 50 | 0 | 30 | 6000 |
| C / 01 | 5920 | 0 | 30 | 50 | 6000 |
| D / 11 full V3 | 5920 | 50 | 30 | 0 | 6000 |

For a future authorized test, prepare each 6,000 uL concentrate master so every source aliquot meets the 10 uL floor; take 600 uL concentrate + 2,400 uL ethanol for each coded 3 mL bottle. Use two independently prepared master sets, anonymous randomized codes, balanced order, and a sealed key. Read at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours. Record free description first; then score LNDL identity, cold shell, lavender hinge, warm seed plausibility, shell-to-seed transition, cedar/vetiver recurrence, airy/dense simultaneity, spatial depth, textural complexion, late identity echo, overall liking, muddiness, harshness, fatigue, pastry/candy drift, lipstick-iris drift, and generic amberwood takeover.

Identity loss rejects an arm before abstract depth. A null or discordant result is `HOLD / NON-INFORMATIVE` at this dose and protocol.

