**Candidate-survival audit:** Cardamom remains the modeled opening leader by a narrow 1.02:1 ratio over Bontoux lavender and therefore survives; this ratio still needs smelling because the natural models are uncertain. Cinnamon Bark EO is `HOLD / BLIND A-B REQUIRED`, not a modeled reject. Cedarwood oil Virginia (OAV 0.269), Benzyl Salicylate (0.294), Hexyl Salicylate (0.255), and Benzyl Benzoate (0.001) survive only as explicit structural/omission-test hypotheses and are not counted as audible complexity. All other current rows are retained for their target-linked functions pending the controlled topology test. Derived/unverified ODT share, model family drift, hot-climate volatility assumptions, and note-tier mismatches keep the authority status at WARN.

## Final claim ceiling

This artifact is a theory formula and controlled-test design. It has not been physically compounded or smelled. No similarity, liking, hedonism, luxury, complexity, depth, three-dimensionality, safety, stability, diffusion, longevity, maturation, or release claim is established.
